  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "StatementTyped.letValue composes expression and pattern typings through the intermediate environment. SequenceTyped.nil/cons are the empty and head/tail rules with well-formed-environment convention, and ProgramTyped requires well-formed classes plus an existential final environment from []. No rule requires that final environment to be empty. This corresponds to the retained-storage semantics and explicit exclusion of scope exit/destruction. Prior expression/binding units define both premises before this composition.",
  "limitations": [
    "Correspondence review compares prose, mathematics, definitions and theorem/example statements; Lean proof validity and command results are separate checks. Listing relevant source-context snapshots records definitions and assumptions consulted, not an audit of every tactic or unrelated declaration.",
    "Finite-map notation uses the documented distinct-key and well-formedness conventions. Raw Lean list representations also admit malformed values; no functional-lookup or preservation claim is made for those outside the stated premises."
